3	// The Web Speech recognition API and speechSynthesis are Window-scoped: they
4	// live on `window`/a document, which an MV3 background service worker does not
5	// have. Referencing them in the worker throws (recognition) or leaves the global
6	// undefined (synthesis) at runtime — a listen or speak that silently never
7	// happens. chrome.tts is the extension-only TTS engine that DOES run in the
8	// worker, so synthesis has a real worker path; recognition has none and must
9	// move to a document context. Repo-state on purpose: a worker that references
10	// one of these is a live break however long ago it merged.
11	//
12	// RELEVANCE FIRST (see engine/checks/README.md "Adding a rule"): a skill check runs on
