3	// The other half of the scheduled-task contract (scheduled-tasks.md, "Every task
4	// declaration carries the full contract" + "The task folder"): the declaration
5	// and the folder it sits in must AGREE. `task-declaration-shape` asserts the
6	// declaration's own shape — that `id` and `agent_instructions` are present and
7	// the enums are legal — and stops at the file's edge; this rule is the
8	// cross-artifact invariant between that file and the tree around it.
9	//
10	// Why it is its own rule rather than more of that one: both faces fail the same
11	// way, and it is the way a shape error does NOT fail. Discovery
12	// (engine/scheduler/discover.mjs) is fail-soft per task — a task whose declared
13	// `id` differs from its directory name is dropped into `errors` and simply never
14	// runs, and a dangling `agent_instructions` hands the executor a worker doc that
15	// isn't there. Nothing goes red; the scheduler keeps reporting healthy runs while
16	// the task is silently absent from every one of them. That is the class this
17	// repo's own canon names as the expensive one, so it is worth catching where it
18	// is cheap: at author time, in the session that wrote the file.
19	//
20	// RELEVANCE FIRST (engine/checks/README.md): gated on a `tasks/<name>/task.mjs`
21	// existing, so the rule is inert on any repo that schedules nothing. Static text
